  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong, cohesive cyber-editorial art direction: disciplined near-black palette, crisp white type, restrained cyan/green/yellow semantics, and clear query-to-outcome hierarchy. The bordered data panel feels polished and adapts without viewport overflow. However, desktop composition leaves excessive dead space and separates the explanation awkwardly from the headline; mobile becomes a very long, repetitive stack with undersized mono labels and metadata. Tablet/mobile headers visibly crop the horizontal navigation, while the mobile header loses the brand name and red-mode action. Header contrast also lacks complete proof at tablet/mobile.",
    "fix": "Tighten the desktop hero into a more balanced grid, compress mobile precedent rows, increase small-label legibility, and redesign the narrow header with a deliberate compact navigation pattern instead of visibly clipped links.",
